@page "/access-denied"

<PageTitle>Access denied · BinTool</PageTitle>

<div class="page-head">
    <h1 class="h3 mb-1">Access denied</h1>
    <p class="text-secondary mb-0">
        You are signed in, but none of your roles carry the permission this page needs.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="card mt-4">
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="mb-2">
            Each page requires a permission, granted by holding a role that carries it. An
            admin can add the permission to one of your roles from <strong>Access
            Control</strong> - and because permissions are baked into the token at sign-in,
            you will need to sign in again afterwards for it to take effect.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary small mb-3">
            The API enforces the same rule, so this is not something a client can work around.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm" href="/">Back to home</a>
    </div>
</div>
